<h2><a id="Presentació" name="Presentació"></a>Presentation and options</h2>

<p>This application imports and exports between the KML format of GoogleEarth and MiraMon.</p>

<!--Aquí inicia la part corresponent a les opcions de de la MSA. Aquesta part s'ha d'editar desde el document WPS (aplicacio.mps).-->
<span id="wpsopcions"/>
<!--Aquí acaba la part corresponent a les opcions de de la MSA editable de el WPS.-->

<p>The application creates a map with a point layer (PNT), which contains the  'Point' type KML objects, a (ARC/NOD) line layer for KML objects of  the 'LineString' type and a layer of polygons that contains the  'Polygon' type objects, if there are any. 'MultiGeometry'  and 'LinearRing' type objects that are not part of a polygon are  ignored. If there is information regarding the z of each vertex, it is also  converted. The layers are not structured topologically.</p>

<p>The 'id' attribute and the 'name', 'description'  y 'styleUrl' elements of each KML object are included. They are all  added to the main table of each layer as thematic attributes under the  names: ID_ENTITAT, NOM, DESCRIPCIO e ID_ESTIL.</p>

<p>The map allows you to open all the layers created with symbolization,  which for lines and polygons depends on the field values 'ID_ESTIL'  and for the points is a radius point 3 with a text with the value of the  'NOM' attribute of the object.</p>

<p>All the objects of any KML file are in latitude/longitude projection with  WGS84 datum, but the application allows you to reproject the map layers to any  of the reference systems described in the MiraMon geodesic tables.</p><p><a href="#MENU"><img src="back.jpg"/></a></p>

